## The 10 always-apply rules (memorize)

These fire on **every task**. Numbered as A001-A010 so per-project
overrides can append A011+ at the bottom.

### Coding quality (the non-negotiables)

- **A001 — TDD by default.** Write the failing test FIRST, see it red,
  then implement until green. Refactor with the test as your safety net.
  No "I'll add tests after." If the change is unit-testable, TDD is not
  optional. Invoke `superpowers:test-driven-development` before any
  implementation. *Why:* the failing-first step is what makes the test
  meaningful; an after-the-fact test only proves what you already wrote.
  **Iron Law: no production code without a failing test first** — wrote
  code first? delete it, start over. (Excuses → [`../../docs/setup/discipline-red-flags.md`](../../docs/setup/discipline-red-flags.md).)
- **A002 — Zero-bug discipline.** Treat every task as a contract: it ships
  green or it doesn't ship. No silent failures, no "I'll fix the edge
  case in a follow-up," no commented-out tests. Edge cases identified
  during impl become tests, not TODOs. If you can't make it green, raise
  the task back as blocked instead of merging yellow. **Iron Law: it
  ships green or it doesn't ship.**
- **A003 — Verification before completion.** Never claim "done" without
  invoking `superpowers:verification-before-completion`. Run the actual
  build + test + smoke command; paste the **real output** into your
  report (not "tests passed"). Evidence before assertions, always.
  **Iron Law: no completion claim without fresh verification evidence
  in this message.**
- **A004 — 6-gate post-delegation review (MANDATORY).** Every coding
  subagent that returns must pass all 6 gates before merge. **Iron Law:
  the subagent's "done" is an input, not evidence** — re-derive from the
  diff + re-run commands.
  Full playbook: [`../../docs/playbooks/post-delegation-review.md`](../../docs/playbooks/post-delegation-review.md).
  1. **Inspect**: `git diff --stat` + read the diff. Never trust the
     subagent's "done" summary.
  2. **Build + Test**: real build + real test in every touched area;
     green is the only acceptable state.
  3. **Boundary / Architecture**: check the diff against the project's own
     boundaries (in `code-style.md` + the N1 rule), reviewed by `senior-tech-lead`.
  4. **Spec-compliance (4a) → Quality (4b)**: 4a FIRST — read the code
     against the D-doc AC list and confirm every AC is implemented and
     nothing extra was built (over/under-build). THEN 4b — dispatch
     `pr-review-toolkit:{code-reviewer, silent-failure-hunter, type-design-analyzer}`
     in a single message (add `:pr-test-analyzer` if tests touched,
     `:comment-analyzer` if comments touched). 4a gates 4b.
  5. **Wiring (L116)**: composition root has the new code; migrations
     applied; instrumentation emits; topics created; contracts in sync.
     Compile-green ≠ feature-wired.
  6. **Integration smoke**: start the system, run the golden path
     end-to-end. If UI changed: run `/design-review` for real-browser
     visual fidelity (green unit/type/lint ≠ correct UI).
- **A005 — Design-doc-first.** Every non-trivial task needs a design doc
  in `docs/designs/sprint-S<N>/D<NNN>-<slug>.md` MERGED before any code
  edit. Sprint file = scope; D-doc = how. Skipping this is the single
  biggest cause of churn. **Iron Law: no code edit before the design doc
  is merged.**

### Delegation & parallelism

- **A006 — Subagent dispatch via the `Agent` tool.** Use `subagent_type`
  to pick the right specialist (`{{AGENT_PREFIX}}-orchestrator`,
  `design-doc-writer`, `senior-tech-lead`, plus any preset agents).
  **Never `claude -p`** — that's an external process per task, no shared
  memory, brittle output, slow iteration.
- **A007 — Parallel safety (4-layer).** When dispatching 2+ subagents in
  one message: (1) declare each agent's allowed paths upfront and grep
  for overlap, (2) `isolation: "worktree"` on every parallel write
  agent, (3) contract-first if the change touches a cross-service
  shape, (4) `TaskCreate` + `addBlocks/addBlockedBy` for any
  dependency. Overlap detected → serialize, don't parallel. Full
  playbook: [`../../docs/playbooks/parallel-conflict-prevention.md`](../../docs/playbooks/parallel-conflict-prevention.md).

### Sources of truth & rhythm

- **A008 — `docs/spec/STATUS.md` + `docs/spec/backlog.md` are
  source-of-truth** for "what's next". Never derive from chat history.
  At sprint close, MOVE prose to `STATUS-archive.md` in the SAME commit
  (do not append to live rows).
- **A009 — Live per-task mini-retro (L036).** After each task passes the
  6-gate review, append a 6-field mini-retro to
  `docs/spec/retros/sprint-S<N>-tasks.md` BEFORE moving on. `/retro`
  aggregates these at sprint close. Deferring retros = losing the
  learning.
- **A010 — LSP-first navigation** (see L147 below). For
  *semantic* questions (what is this symbol, where is it defined, who
  calls it) → built-in LSP (`documentSymbol`, `hover`, `findReferences`,
  `goToDefinition`). For *text* search (regex in YAML, cross-language
  string) → Grep. See [`lsp-first.md`](./lsp-first.md).

