## Cross-cutting lessons (L###) that bite often

The highest-leverage few are summarized here; the full registry (with
trigger conditions) is [`../../docs/setup/lesson-trigger-map.md`](../../docs/setup/lesson-trigger-map.md).
Each lesson carries its own one-line summary — applying them needs no
external brain.

- **L020 — Selector contract.** Every `data-testid` ships in the D-doc
  selector map BEFORE UI + E2E impl. Mismatch class kills hours.
- **L035 — Touched-files matrix.** Every D-doc declares which files it
  touches. Used by `/dispatch-parallel` Conflict Radar (Layer 1).
- **L076 — D-doc ≥500L for non-trivial impl tasks.** Empirical zero-fix
  threshold across 48+ sprints. Light template OK for surgical sweeps.
- **L087 — Backlog sync per-task** (see A009 above for retro).
- **L116 — Composition-root wiring.** Post-delegation, grep
  `cmd/<svc>/main.go` (or your composition root) for every new
  use-case + adapter + migration. **Compile-green ≠ feature-wired.**
- **L147 — LSP-first** (see A010 above).
- **L149 — AC type-contradiction scan.** Before authoring a D-doc, LSP
  `hover` every type the AC mentions; catch contradictions early.
- **L156 — LSP type verification** before pasting code templates into a
  D-doc. Hallucinated types = rework.
- **L101 — Evidence-based.** Curl-verify, never fix from code reading
  alone. The compiler doesn't know what production is doing.
- **L182 — Visual fidelity ≠ structural review.** Unit + accessibility
  tree snapshots can pass while pixels / spacing / theme tokens are
  wrong. UI sprints MUST run `/design-review` (3-lens visual gate)
  before promote.

